WEBVTT

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:16.130
<b>Episode 26</b>

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:16.130
<b>Madness and Darkness and...</b>

00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:26.880
<i>What?</i>

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:29.600
<i>What the hell is he?</i>

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:36.070
<i>Who does he think I am?</i>

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:40.110
<i>I am this country's king.</i>

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:44.210
<i>Until now, all have bowed 
before me, without exception.</i>

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:50.540
<i>Be it ministers of the cabinet, 
organized crime bosses, police,</i>

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:55.820
<i>bureaucrats, banks, zaibatsus, 
religious leaders.</i>

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:02.080
<i>I ruled over them all of them.</i>

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:06.330
<i>And yet this punk... this brat!</i>

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:09.340
<i>It's ridiculous!</i>

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:11.330
<i>This cannot be allowed.</i>

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:15.330
<i>It simply can't be allowed.</i>

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:18.760
<i>You will bow down before me.</i>

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:22.350
If he discards the 4 of circles, 
Washizu will be in tenpai.

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:35.800
<i>This 4 of circles is most likely 
the enemy's winning tile.</i>

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:38.300
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:41.530
<i>I can't discard it.</i>

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:45.540
You're actually quite the 
coward, Washizu Iwao.

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:50.170
So then all I have to do is target...

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:51.540
those weak spots.

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:53.510
<i>That's insane.</i>

00:02:53.510 --> 00:02:55.450
<i>I am the king!</i>

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:57.050
<i>The king!</i>

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:58.940
<i>You peasant.</i>

00:03:00.670 --> 00:03:01.850
<i>I'll make this pass.</i>

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:03.290
<i>I'll make it!</i>

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:11.410
Ron.

00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:12.260
5,200.

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:17.500
<i>This is horrible.</i>

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:20.330
<i>He couldn't even keep 
himself from dealing into</i>

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:21.240
<i>that obvious 4, 7 of circles wait.</i>

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:25.240
<i>He has completely lost himself.</i>

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:28.430
It's true for ordinary Mahjong as well,

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:32.250
but in Washizu Mahjong, keeping a 
cool head is even more crucial.

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:35.220
Specifically, keeping 
control of your own fear.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:40.750
Should you waver here, you will 
sink into a bog of endless doubts.

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:43.180
You will be led astray by illusions

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:46.430
and either destroy your hand by 
wandering off into the void

00:03:46.430 --> 00:03:49.530
or make a bold move 
just to get away from that.

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:56.510
It's a reactionary failure.

00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:02.140
Once it starts, 
there is no stopping it.

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:05.250
Ron.

00:04:07.090 --> 00:04:09.490
He will keep falling and falling.

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:16.480
Right now, Washizu looks exactly 
like the young men he's killed until now.

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:20.180
They were also controlled 
by their own fear.

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:21.800
They lost their balance 
and started a chain

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:23.800
of outrageous discards and 
giving up on the game.

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:29.210
They died, having lost the sense of 
what is normal and what is abnormal.

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:33.710
This is Washizu's first taste of that,

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:37.710
that essence of Washizu Mahjong.

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:51.930
<i>I can't discard the 7 of bamboo.</i>

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:55.890
That's right.

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:59.350
Washizu has played Washizu 
Mahjong many, many times,

00:04:59.350 --> 00:05:02.440
but he has never participated 
in the truest sense of the term.

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:06.290
While his opponent fought for his life,

00:05:06.290 --> 00:05:09.080
Washizu alone always stood protected.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:12.810
By his overwhelming funds.

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:17.050
It never was a fair fight.

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:19.050
A handicapped fight.

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:22.810
Or rather, for Washizu, 
the battle called Washizu Mahjong

00:05:22.810 --> 00:05:25.920
existed in another dimension.

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:27.060
In other words,

00:05:28.350 --> 00:05:29.060
a hunt.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:34.070
A hunt where he hunted down a wild, 
running beast with an ultimate weapon.

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:38.940
Far from being a deathmatch, 
it was one-sided murder.

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:44.020
Washizu is the one who kills.

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:46.210
His opponent is the 
one who gets killed.

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:51.310
That is what Washizu 
Mahjong was to Washizu.

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:55.820
But now...

00:05:57.710 --> 00:06:01.560
a beast beyond his wildest 
imagination has appeared.

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:09.360
Not only does this beast not 
fear death, it also happens...

00:06:12.450 --> 00:06:14.570
to attack Washizu.

00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:21.190
It wants to kill Washizu.

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:23.860
<i>Why?</i>

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:26.790
<i>Why does this man exist?</i>

00:06:28.770 --> 00:06:30.520
<i>Why does this...</i>

00:06:33.150 --> 00:06:34.260
<i>demon... exist?</i>

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:38.180
<i>I can't deal any bamboo tile.</i>

00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:41.000
Ron.

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:43.620
Tanyao, one dora.

00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:44.500
2,900.

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:57.700
In the end, Washizu lost the third match

00:06:57.700 --> 00:07:00.430
and then the fourth, in succession.

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:03.190
At his wit's end, he falls apart.

00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:05.350
After the third match,

00:07:05.350 --> 00:07:07.830
the gap between him 
and Akagi is 107,000 points.

00:07:07.830 --> 00:07:10.440
At the end of the fourth, 
it's 63,000 points.

00:07:10.440 --> 00:07:12.020
Altogether, that's 170,000 points.

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:16.970
Adding in the direct hit 
and tsumo bonuses makes a

00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:18.740
grand total of 195,000 points.

00:07:18.740 --> 00:07:22.600
In other words, 
Washizu has lost 195 million yen,

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:26.740
and his total loss amounts 
to 313.5 million yen.

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:32.950
This amount in 1965 would equate 
to about 3.2 billion yen today.

00:07:34.230 --> 00:07:38.780
At the start of the game, 
Washizu's 500 million seemed endless,

00:07:38.780 --> 00:07:40.960
but he has now fallen 
under 200 million.

00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:44.450
On the other hand, the amount 
of blood Akagi lost in the third

00:07:44.450 --> 00:07:46.140
and fourth matches only 
amounts to 300 CCs.

00:07:46.550 --> 00:07:48.510
It is a miracle he was 
able to keep it so low,

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:52.070
but he has already lost 
a total of 1,400 CCs.

00:07:56.340 --> 00:07:57.950
Akagi versus Washizu.

00:07:58.470 --> 00:08:01.110
This battle wagering their 
death and destruction

00:08:01.110 --> 00:08:02.980
has now been going 
for over three hours.

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:06.080
The trend has been set.

00:08:06.620 --> 00:08:08.680
Washizu, four consecutive losses.

00:08:09.740 --> 00:08:11.280
<i>This is harsh.</i>

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:13.190
<i>More than that...</i>

00:08:13.950 --> 00:08:15.620
<i>is it over?</i>

00:08:16.150 --> 00:08:20.890
<i>But that kid really is immeasurable.</i>

00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:23.910
<i>Not once has he dealt 
into Washizu's hand.</i>

00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:29.270
<i>All of the blood he's lost has been 
due to Washizu-sama's tsumo wins.</i>

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:32.570
<i>Can this even be possible?</i>

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:34.350
<i>He is like a demon.</i>

00:08:35.850 --> 00:08:41.260
<i>Thinking of the fatal amount though, 
he's already lost 1,400 CCs.</i>

00:08:41.260 --> 00:08:42.970
<i>It'll only take a small push now.</i>

00:08:44.170 --> 00:08:45.940
<i>Not even a mangan.</i>

00:08:45.940 --> 00:08:48.580
<i>A direct hit of 5,200 would kill him.</i>

00:08:49.530 --> 00:08:55.440
<i>But that's only because he has yet 
to transfer any of his blood back.</i>

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:58.850
<i>Looking at his overwhelming 
skill and luck,</i>

00:08:58.850 --> 00:09:01.030
<i>it's deceptive to say 
"only a small push."</i>

00:09:01.950 --> 00:09:03.200
<i>That's an illusion.</i>

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:05.360
<i>One must not be fooled by it.</i>

00:09:05.360 --> 00:09:08.270
<i>This is the strategy of 
the demon called Akagi.</i>

00:09:08.720 --> 00:09:13.380
<i>It beckons us on to the next stage 
of the battle, to our destruction.</i>

00:09:13.810 --> 00:09:16.480
<i>If we keep going,</i>

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:19.990
<i>he won't have to take any more 
drastic measures to keep us playing.</i>

00:09:20.830 --> 00:09:23.490
<i>Should he lose any more blood, 
he will naturally transfer some back.</i>

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:29.670
<i>If that happens, Washizu-sama won't 
even have a 1% chance of winning.</i>

00:09:30.690 --> 00:09:32.230
<i>This is the end.</i>

00:09:32.700 --> 00:09:34.610
<i>It would be wise to end it here.</i>

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:40.530
<i>The 300 million loss hurts, of course, 
but there's nothing we can do.</i>

00:09:41.510 --> 00:09:44.260
<i>Looking at it another way, 
we still have 200 million left.</i>

00:09:44.970 --> 00:09:49.410
<i>In a regular match, he probably 
would have taken all of the 500 million.</i>

00:09:50.430 --> 00:09:52.910
<i>We stop every two matches and we have</i>

00:09:52.910 --> 00:09:57.040
<i>the power to get out of the 
game at any of those stops.</i>

00:09:57.660 --> 00:10:00.300
<i>This privilege will keep us alive.</i>

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:04.260
<i>Looking back, putting in this 
condition was priceless.</i>

00:10:04.590 --> 00:10:06.140
<i>Because we survived.</i>

00:10:06.600 --> 00:10:09.030
<i>Wounded, but still standing.</i>

00:10:15.620 --> 00:10:16.770
It's over.

00:10:17.430 --> 00:10:20.280
He's not going to keep going.

00:10:20.670 --> 00:10:22.650
The game has been decided.

00:10:22.650 --> 00:10:28.020
Well, we didn't get the full 500 
million, but this is enough.

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:30.730
I'll be honest, I'm relieved.

00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:35.690
The money was one thing, but if we'd 
lost, I would've lost one of my arms!

00:10:35.690 --> 00:10:36.460
Hey.

00:10:36.460 --> 00:10:38.020
Get ready to leave.

00:10:38.020 --> 00:10:38.530
Yes, sir.

00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:40.760
What are you talking about?

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:46.740
It's not over yet.

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:50.970
Washizu will keep going.

00:10:52.280 --> 00:10:54.820
What are you talking about?!

00:10:54.820 --> 00:10:55.770
That's crazy!

00:10:55.770 --> 00:10:56.710
It's not possible!

00:10:57.180 --> 00:10:58.800
This is the time to stop!

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:01.550
What possible reason could 
we have to keep going?

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:04.120
Besides, Washizu's exhausted.

00:11:04.120 --> 00:11:06.530
He can't even stand up.

00:11:06.530 --> 00:11:09.220
Of course, we can't continue <i>this</i> way.

00:11:10.410 --> 00:11:13.460
He needs a compromise, 
from our side.

00:11:13.460 --> 00:11:14.720
What?

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:19.980
So far, all of my wins have 
been surprise attacks,

00:11:19.980 --> 00:11:23.070
taking advantage of Washizu's 
misunderstandings and his carelessness.

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:27.580
He got caught up in it 
and started to sink.

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:33.310
Once he noticed, it was irreversible.

00:11:33.310 --> 00:11:36.430
He hasn't fought me directly yet.

00:11:36.430 --> 00:11:38.990
Which means he hasn't fought 
me at his full capacity yet.

00:11:40.990 --> 00:11:44.560
But if we keep going, it will be different.

00:11:45.500 --> 00:11:48.060
It'll be a real face-off.

00:11:48.620 --> 00:11:51.800
There will be no carelessness 
nor underestimating.

00:11:52.730 --> 00:11:55.800
I want to fight him like that.

00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:57.660
In a real face-off.

00:11:59.660 --> 00:12:04.040
Or I would leave here, not knowing 
what the real Washizu is like.

00:12:04.830 --> 00:12:09.550
It would end without me seeing the 
true nature and power of Washizu.

00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:14.730
Seeing him like that, 
he looks just like a lone rat.

00:12:15.440 --> 00:12:17.560
The truth is, at one point, 
I thought of him like that.

00:12:18.720 --> 00:12:21.560
Is it possible though?

00:12:22.270 --> 00:12:24.790
For such a small person, such a rat,

00:12:24.790 --> 00:12:29.570
to gain the title of the king ruling 
from the shadows in just one generation?

00:12:29.900 --> 00:12:33.310
Could he have risen to such 
a feared, lofty position?

00:12:34.700 --> 00:12:35.980
No.

00:12:35.980 --> 00:12:39.080
An ordinary person cannot aggrandize 
himself to that degree.

00:12:39.080 --> 00:12:40.530
There's something to him.

00:12:41.040 --> 00:12:45.730
Washizu's core is not 
the rat we see now.

00:12:46.710 --> 00:12:48.590
There is something deeper within him.

00:12:49.720 --> 00:12:53.310
And if that's true, we must see it.

00:12:53.310 --> 00:12:57.170
That thing deep within, 
Washizu's true self,

00:12:57.170 --> 00:12:58.330
his source of power.

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:01.330
So then...

00:13:03.820 --> 00:13:05.540
Can you push that for me?

00:13:07.040 --> 00:13:08.040
Akagi...

00:13:08.880 --> 00:13:10.570
Hey, wait.

00:13:10.570 --> 00:13:12.780
What are you thinking?

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:17.090
What?

00:13:17.090 --> 00:13:18.280
What do you want?

00:13:18.970 --> 00:13:21.100
Break time is over.

00:13:21.100 --> 00:13:22.690
Get up.

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:24.910
It's time to start.

00:13:26.520 --> 00:13:28.040
Stop this.

00:13:28.040 --> 00:13:30.230
That is not possible.

00:13:30.610 --> 00:13:34.240
Washizu-sama is not in 
a condition to continue!

00:13:35.820 --> 00:13:37.230
You okay with that, Washizu?

00:13:37.730 --> 00:13:40.100
Having this punk talk for you?

00:13:41.360 --> 00:13:43.860
Here, I'll wake you up.

00:13:46.750 --> 00:13:48.850
I'm going to borrow one of these.

00:13:53.490 --> 00:13:55.220
What the hell are you...

00:13:55.220 --> 00:13:55.820
Hey!

00:13:58.410 --> 00:14:00.270
Akagi, what are you doing?

00:14:00.270 --> 00:14:01.560
That's your blood!

00:14:01.910 --> 00:14:03.410
You need to get that transfused back!

00:14:09.980 --> 00:14:11.000
You idiot!

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:12.270
What the hell are you doing?

00:14:12.840 --> 00:14:14.220
That's dirty!

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:17.680
That thing is not sterilized, Akagi!

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:19.280
I don't care.

00:14:19.660 --> 00:14:21.280
What do you mean?!

00:14:21.710 --> 00:14:22.980
Hey!

00:14:22.980 --> 00:14:25.010
I mean this...

00:14:29.190 --> 00:14:30.290
What?!

00:14:30.290 --> 00:14:31.290
You idiot!

00:14:31.290 --> 00:14:32.920
Hurry up and get that out!

00:14:41.760 --> 00:14:42.860
You moron!

00:14:44.060 --> 00:14:45.970
How could you do that?

00:14:47.100 --> 00:14:49.650
<i>H-He's crazy.</i>

00:14:49.650 --> 00:14:51.210
<i>What is this?</i>

00:14:51.210 --> 00:14:54.110
<i>Where is the good in this?</i>

00:14:55.970 --> 00:14:57.850
You awake now, Washizu?

00:14:58.870 --> 00:15:00.130
I'm throwing it out.

00:15:00.130 --> 00:15:04.350
As you can see, I'm throwing away the 
1,400 CCs of blood I've lost thus far.

00:15:05.110 --> 00:15:06.630
We'll go on from here.

00:15:07.090 --> 00:15:08.890
How about matches five and six?

00:15:09.310 --> 00:15:10.090
Akagi!

00:15:10.740 --> 00:15:11.840
You idiot!

00:15:11.840 --> 00:15:12.780
What are you saying?

00:15:12.780 --> 00:15:14.090
Take that back!

00:15:14.090 --> 00:15:16.330
I'm not going to let you do this.

00:15:16.330 --> 00:15:19.090
What happens now?

00:15:19.630 --> 00:15:23.840
What happens to the blood I 
draw after this, when I tsumo?

00:15:24.510 --> 00:15:26.150
I don't need that, either.

00:15:26.150 --> 00:15:28.550
You can throw it away 
as soon as you draw it.

00:15:28.550 --> 00:15:29.480
Akagi!

00:15:29.480 --> 00:15:32.850
Are you even aware of what 
you're saying right now?!

00:15:33.610 --> 00:15:35.580
This is suicide!

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:36.680
Akagi!

00:15:44.340 --> 00:15:46.090
300 CCs more.

00:15:47.530 --> 00:15:51.060
I want you to draw 300 
more CCs right now.

00:15:51.600 --> 00:15:54.060
As a bonus.

00:15:54.060 --> 00:15:55.300
You idiot.

00:15:57.390 --> 00:16:00.040
Looks like you're getting 
back into it, Washizu.

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:01.530
That's more like you.

00:16:01.530 --> 00:16:02.550
Hey!

00:16:03.710 --> 00:16:05.340
But I can't do that.

00:16:05.340 --> 00:16:07.490
My blood is my life.

00:16:07.490 --> 00:16:12.940
You can only take it by 
winning it from me in a game.

00:16:19.710 --> 00:16:25.490
I just wanted to see how far I 
could get by pushing my luck.

00:16:25.490 --> 00:16:28.570
But you're pretty stingy, Akagi.

00:16:29.950 --> 00:16:31.320
Very well.

00:16:31.320 --> 00:16:34.570
For your arrogance in throwing 
away your own blood...

00:16:34.570 --> 00:16:36.320
For that conceit...

00:16:36.320 --> 00:16:38.310
I'll kill you.

00:16:38.310 --> 00:16:39.960
Washizu-sama!

00:16:39.960 --> 00:16:42.050
Don't worry.

00:16:44.370 --> 00:16:46.280
Now, let's go on.

00:16:46.280 --> 00:16:47.840
Washizu-sama!

00:16:50.790 --> 00:16:52.130
But...

00:16:53.080 --> 00:16:54.290
It's fine.

00:16:54.290 --> 00:16:56.910
There is nothing to fear.

00:16:56.910 --> 00:17:00.030
Now I know what I must do.

00:17:00.030 --> 00:17:03.770
I wasn't using the right 
strategy before now.

00:17:04.130 --> 00:17:06.920
To put it short, 
that man is utterly mad.

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:09.510
He's a psycho with a death wish.

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:11.530
Just think about it.

00:17:11.530 --> 00:17:15.510
He's already lost 1,400 CCs of blood.

00:17:15.510 --> 00:17:17.610
He is literally one 
step away from death.

00:17:17.610 --> 00:17:20.610
One more push would be enough.

00:17:20.610 --> 00:17:24.270
That is undoubtedly true, 
but that man, he is...

00:17:25.760 --> 00:17:28.060
Just watch.

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:29.260
I'll win.

00:17:29.810 --> 00:17:32.460
I won't even have to go 
until the sixth match.

00:17:32.460 --> 00:17:38.730
I'll kill him sometime in the 
East round of the fifth match.

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:46.640
If there is any justice in the world.

00:17:51.350 --> 00:17:52.510
And yet...

00:17:54.520 --> 00:17:57.050
they seem rather lonely.

00:17:57.050 --> 00:17:57.800
You.

00:17:57.800 --> 00:17:58.510
Sir?

00:18:00.040 --> 00:18:02.330
Come with me.

00:18:10.070 --> 00:18:11.230
<i>This is unbelievable.</i>

00:18:11.690 --> 00:18:14.470
<i>What the hell are you doing?</i>

00:18:14.470 --> 00:18:17.840
<i>You should've stopped 
while you were ahead.</i>

00:18:19.210 --> 00:18:22.210
<i>That is the natural order of 
things, that would make sense.</i>

00:18:22.680 --> 00:18:25.950
<i>There's no reason to force 
it into the next match!</i>

00:18:26.570 --> 00:18:30.680
<i>Not to mention that you 
threw away all your blood!</i>

00:18:32.160 --> 00:18:34.420
<i>You're beyond crazy!</i>

00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:37.330
<i>You're marching off to your own death.</i>

00:18:38.270 --> 00:18:44.060
<i>Washizu said it: this time, it's not 
about being this or that kind of genius.</i>

00:18:44.060 --> 00:18:46.440
<i>It's not about that at all.</i>

00:18:46.440 --> 00:18:47.930
<i>You're a lunatic.</i>

00:18:47.930 --> 00:18:50.870
<i>Nothing but a lunatic with a death wish.</i>

00:18:51.530 --> 00:18:53.100
<i>I misjudged you.</i>

00:18:53.930 --> 00:18:58.490
<i>This guy is beyond anything 
we can conceptualize.</i>

00:18:58.490 --> 00:19:00.410
<i>An outlier.</i>

00:19:01.830 --> 00:19:03.280
<i>A lunatic.</i>

00:19:03.920 --> 00:19:08.420
<i>At this rate, I'll get dragged 
down with this lunatic.</i>

00:19:10.190 --> 00:19:11.920
<i>Straight down into hell.</i>

00:19:22.170 --> 00:19:23.640
What is that?

00:19:27.670 --> 00:19:31.110
My last secret savings of 100 million.

00:19:31.110 --> 00:19:32.840
What?!

00:19:34.700 --> 00:19:38.550
With this addition, 
I have 300 million left.

00:19:39.600 --> 00:19:43.050
With this, I'm safe.

00:19:43.050 --> 00:19:48.810
I can go forward in the game, 
knowing I'm protected.

00:19:48.810 --> 00:19:55.300
And I'll draw that last 
600 CCs of your blood!

00:19:57.980 --> 00:19:59.800
There are no exceptions.

00:20:00.630 --> 00:20:05.040
Everyone is equal in 
dying after 2,000 CCs.

00:20:05.040 --> 00:20:06.540
You will die.

00:20:11.570 --> 00:20:13.360
I'm sorry I kept you waiting.

00:20:13.360 --> 00:20:18.870
Then let us begin, Akagi Shigeru!

00:20:24.710 --> 00:20:27.910
The genius wagering a 
meaningless death, Akagi Shigeru,

00:20:27.910 --> 00:20:30.620
and the king of the shadows 
wagering his ruin, Washizu Iwao,

00:20:30.620 --> 00:20:34.040
are yet to reach the 
conclusion of their battle.

00:20:34.410 --> 00:20:39.080
This all happened on August 11th, 1965.

00:20:45.590 --> 00:20:52.100
And eventually, this battle will 
be handed down as a legend.

00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:52.100
1999 Summer
